@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `usca-further-limbs`

-- Tests of usca-further-limbs.l4 (Gov. Code § 6700(b), § 6801, § 6808(a) and (c), § 9606, § 16.5(d), (e), (f)).  Each expected value is decided from the section cited above the assertion,
-- before the run.  A failing assertion is a finding.

§ `Gov. Code § 6700(b): a memorandum of understanding that conflicts with the holiday section`

-- In a conflict the memorandum controls without further legislative action; if its provisions require the expenditure of funds, they are not effective unless approved in the annual Budget Act.
#ASSERT `the memorandum of understanding controls over Gov. Code § 6700` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `the memorandum of understanding controls over Gov. Code § 6700` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `the memorandum of understanding controls over Gov. Code § 6700` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the memorandum of understanding controls over Gov. Code § 6700` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- With no conflict the subdivision does not speak.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the memorandum of understanding controls over Gov. Code § 6700` FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `the memorandum of understanding controls over Gov. Code § 6700` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `the memorandum of understanding controls over Gov. Code § 6700` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `the memorandum of understanding controls over Gov. Code § 6700` FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `further legislative action is needed before the memorandum of understanding controls` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`further legislative action is needed before the memorandum of understanding controls` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `further legislative action is needed before the memorandum of understanding controls` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `further legislative action is needed before the memorandum of understanding controls` FALSE FALSE

§ `Gov. Code § 6801: January 1 is the first day of the year after 1752`

#ASSERT `the day reckoned as the first day of the year` 1753 EQUALS YMD 1753 1 1
#ASSERT `the day reckoned as the first day of the year` 1900 EQUALS YMD 1900 1 1
#ASSERT `the day reckoned as the first day of the year` 2000 EQUALS YMD 2000 1 1
#ASSERT `the day reckoned as the first day of the year` 2026 EQUALS YMD 2026 1 1
-- 1752 itself and the years before it: the text does not say.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day reckoned as the first day of the year` 1752
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day reckoned as the first day of the year` 1751
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day reckoned as the first day of the year` 1700

§ `Gov. Code § 6808(a): the standard time within the state`

#ASSERT `the standard time within the state is that of` `the fifth zone designated by federal law as Pacific standard time`
#ASSERT NOT (`the standard time within the state is that of` `another zone`)
-- The offset is in 15 U.S.C. §§ 261 and 263, not deposited.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the offset of the standard time within the state from Coordinated Universal Time in hours in the year` 2026

§ `Gov. Code § 6808(c): the Legislature's power to amend the section`

#ASSERT `Gov. Code § 6808(c) lets the Legislature make the amendment` `a change to the dates and times of the daylight saving time period` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `Gov. Code § 6808(c) lets the Legislature make the amendment` `a change to the dates and times of the daylight saving time period` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Gov. Code § 6808(c) lets the Legislature make the amendment` `a change to the dates and times of the daylight saving time period` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Gov. Code § 6808(c) lets the Legislature make the amendment` `a change to the dates and times of the daylight saving time period` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Gov. Code § 6808(c) lets the Legislature make the amendment` `a change to the dates and times of the daylight saving time period` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Year-round daylight saving time needs federal authorization and a two-thirds vote; consistency of a change of dates is not the test.
#ASSERT `Gov. Code § 6808(c) lets the Legislature make the amendment` `the year-round application of daylight saving time` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `Gov. Code § 6808(c) lets the Legislature make the amendment` `the year-round application of daylight saving time` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Gov. Code § 6808(c) lets the Legislature make the amendment` `the year-round application of daylight saving time` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Gov. Code § 6808(c) lets the Legislature make the amendment` `the year-round application of daylight saving time` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `Gov. Code § 6808(c) lets the Legislature make the amendment` `another amendment` TRUE TRUE TRUE

§ `Gov. Code § 9606: persons act in contemplation of the power of repeal`

#ASSERT `the person acts in contemplation of the power of repeal` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the person acts in contemplation of the power of repeal` FALSE)

§ `Gov. Code § 16.5(d): digital signature`

#ASSERT `a digital signature in the sense of Gov. Code § 16.5(d)` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a digital signature in the sense of Gov. Code § 16.5(d)` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a digital signature in the sense of Gov. Code § 16.5(d)` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a digital signature in the sense of Gov. Code § 16.5(d)` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `it is an electronic signature for purposes of Gov. Code § 16.5` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `it is an electronic signature for purposes of Gov. Code § 16.5` FALSE

§ `Gov. Code § 16.5(e): the right to use and accept an electronic signature`

#ASSERT NOT (`Gov. Code § 16.5 limits the right of a public entity or government agency to use and accept it` TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `Gov. Code § 16.5 limits the right of a public entity or government agency to use and accept it` FALSE

§ `Gov. Code § 16.5(f): the Secretary of State's regulations`

#ASSERT `the Secretary of State's regulations to implement Gov. Code § 16.5 apply to the use of` `a digital signature` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the Secretary of State's regulations to implement Gov. Code § 16.5 apply to the use of` `a digital signature` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the Secretary of State's regulations to implement Gov. Code § 16.5 apply to the use of` `another type of electronic signature authorized in the Uniform Electronic Transactions Act` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the Secretary of State's regulations to implement Gov. Code § 16.5 apply to the use of` `something else` TRUE)

-- assertions written: 46
